[0.169, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat it involves:\u001b[21G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mSpace::CruiseProfile\u001b[42G\u001b[39mgets\u001b[47Gan\u001b[50Goptional\u001b[59G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249msustainedSeconds\u001b[39m.\u001b[77GThe\u001b[81Gship\u001b[86Gholds\u001b[92Gthe\u001b[96Gsustained\u001b[106Gacceleration\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bfor that long, split evenly between the two\u001b[47Ge\u001b[49Gds after the boost, and coasts in between.\u001b[92G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCruiseSeconds\u001b[107G\u001b[39mnd\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCruiseCovered\u001b[39m need clos\u001b[27Gd forms for\u001b[41Gat profile. \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCheckCruiseDrive\u001b[39m must refuse negative or non-finite seconds,\u001b[114Gand\u001b[118Ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bprofile with no speed to coast at. A world saved mid-coast has to arrive at the same hash as the world it wa\u001b[112G s\u001b[115Gved\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bf\u001b[6Gm, \u001b[10Gvery pinned hash has to\u001b[34Ghold,\u001b[40Gand the sample's drive cruises on the new profile once.\u001b[96G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mModel advice:\u001b[17G\u001b[22mOpus,\u001b[23Ghigh\u001b[28Geffort,\u001b[36Gfor\u001b[40Gthe\u001b[44Gdesign\u001b[51Gand\u001b[55Gthe\u001b[59Gclosed-form\u001b[71Gmaths\u001b[77Gat\u001b[80Gleast.\u001b[87GThe\u001b[91Gchange\u001b[98Gtouches\u001b[106Gthe\u001b[110Gsave's\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bshape (a new optional field, plus the stat\u001b[46G needed to rest\u001b[62Gr\u001b[64G mid-coas\u001b[74G) and\u001b[80Gthe determinism of the drive's\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bintegration,\u001b[16Gwhere \u001b[23G weak \u001b[30Gesign is co\u001b[43Gly to undo. Onc\u001b[59G \u001b[61Ghe hea\u001b[68Ger contr\u001b[77Gct\u001b[80Gand\u001b[84Gthe formulas are fixed, Sonnet\u001b[115Ghigh\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcould wr\u001b[12Gte the t\u001b[21Gsts and\u001b[29Grun the gate. The implementation i