[0.069, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mplanets; politically banned by nuclear treaties.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNuclear Salt-Water Rocket (NSWR)    1–2g for hours (continuously detonating uranium-salt water in an open magnetic \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bnozzle)    Moderate (engineering nightmare, no new physics needed)    Exhaust is an intensely radioactive plasma jet;\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bone fuel tank leak destroys the ship.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BMagneto-Inertial / Pulsed Fusion    0.1–1g bursts (magnetic compression of deuterium-tritium or helium-3 pellets)    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BModerate to High (likely for interplanetary cargo by the 2100s)    Better suited to steady 0.05g–0.2g burns rather \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthan continuous 1–2g \"grav-drive\" cruising.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BAntimatter-Catalyzed / Beam-Core    1–2g continuous (closest real-world equivalent to The Expanse's Epstein Drive)   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BVery Low within 150 years    Producing and storing tons of antimatter, plus radiating terawatts of heat, remains far\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbeyond 22nd-century engineering.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BThe Realistic 150-Year Outcome\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BBy the late 2100s, a corsair-sized cargo ship won't cruise at 1g for weeks at a time. Instead, it would likely cruise\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Befficiently at 0.05g to 0.2g using a pulsed fusion drive (still cutting a Mars trip down to a couple of weeks), \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwhile keeping an auxiliary chemical or nuclear thermal thruster in reserve for short 1–2g combat or docking burns.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BWould you like to calculate travel times to Mars or Jupiter under a 0.1g vs. 1g burn, or explore how ship radiator \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdesigns and magnetic nozzles deal with terawatt-level heat?\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BShow Code\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;215;119;87mEnchanting\u001b[38;2;235;159;127m…\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.015, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[79C\u001b[20B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · \u001b[38;2;163;163;163mthinking with high effort\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m)\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.003, "o", "\u001b]0;◑ jettison-0013\u0007"]
